  "question": {
    "text": "The points&nbsp;<math><mi>A</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;lie on the parabola <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></math>, such that the chord <math><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> subtends <math><mn>90</mn><mo>°</mo></math> at the origin, then the length of the chord&nbsp;<math><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> is equal to",
